# Book Reading App

> A focused, distraction-free eBook reader for Android with bookmarks, search, and adaptive themes.

![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Android-3DDC84?style=flat&logo=android&logoColor=white)
![Language](https://img.shields.io/badge/Language-Kotlin-7F52FF?style=flat&logo=kotlin&logoColor=white)
![Monetisation](https://img.shields.io/badge/Ads-AdMob-FFCA28?style=flat&logo=google&logoColor=black)

## Overview

An Android eBook reader built for comfort and simplicity. Users can bookmark pages, search content, and switch between day and night modes — all with lightweight local storage and revenue-generating ads that don't disrupt the reading experience.

## Features

- **Bookmarking** — Save any page and jump back to it instantly; persists across sessions
- **Page search** — Navigate directly to any page
- **Day / Night mode** — Adaptive themes for comfortable reading in any lighting
- **AdMob integration** — Non-intrusive ads for passive monetisation
- **Lightweight storage** — Local bookmark sync with zero data loss

## Tech Stack

| Component    | Technology                        |
|--------------|-----------------------------------|
| Language     | Kotlin                            |
| Architecture | MVVM                              |
| Storage      | Room Database / SharedPreferences |
| Ads          | Google AdMob                      |
| UI           | XML Layouts / ViewBinding         |
| Build        | Gradle (Kotlin DSL), Android SDK  |

## Getting Started

1. Clone the repo
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/Areesha555/Book_Reading_App.git
   ```
2. Open in **Android Studio**
3. Add your AdMob App ID to `AndroidManifest.xml`:
   ```xml
   <meta-data
       android:name="com.google.android.gms.ads.APPLICATION_ID"
       android:value="YOUR_ADMOB_APP_ID"/>
   ```
4. Run on emulator or physical device (API 21+)

